\name{proteins_annotate_go}
\alias{proteins_annotate_go}
\title{Annotate MetaMorpheus protein groups with Gene Ontology terms, keeping every member}
\usage{
proteins_annotate_go(groups, database, go_obo, category_map = NULL,
  skip_unknown_go_ids = FALSE, out = NULL, categories_out = NULL, limit = NULL,
  offset = 0, timeout = NULL)
}
\arguments{
\item{groups}{A MetaMorpheus protein-group table: \code{AllQuantifiedProteinGroups.tsv},
  \code{AllProteinGroups.tsv} (a search without quantification), or one file's
  \code{<file>_ProteinGroups.tsv}.}

\item{database}{The UniProt XML (\code{.xml} or \code{.xml.gz}) whose GO terms annotate the members: the
  proteome the search used. A FASTA is refused, because it carries no GO and every group would
  read \code{"no_go_terms"} whatever the proteins are.}

\item{go_obo}{A go.obo file. It must exist; nothing is fetched.}

\item{category_map}{Optional: your own term-to-category map in mzLib's format
  (\code{#!category_map_format 1}, \code{#!map_name}, \code{#!map_version}, then \code{category}, \code{subcategory} and
  \code{anchor_go_id} columns). mzLib ships no vocabulary. Adds \code{categories}.}

\item{skip_unknown_go_ids}{\code{FALSE} (the default) fails when the database cites a GO id the
  ontology release lacks - usually a UniProt release newer than the go.obo - and names every
  missing id. \code{TRUE} drops each such id and lists it in \code{unresolved_go_ids}.}

\item{out}{Write the \strong{whole} table here with mzLib's own \code{GoAnnotationTsv} writer, provenance
  header included, whatever \code{limit} and \code{offset} are. Must end in \code{.tsv}. For a large run pair it
  with \code{limit = 0}, so only the summary comes back.}

\item{categories_out}{Write the category table here with mzLib's \code{GoCategoryTsv} writer. Must
  end in \code{.tsv}, and needs \code{category_map}.}

\item{limit}{At most this many rows (rows, not groups) in \code{annotations}. \code{NULL}, the default,
  returns them all. Never shortens \code{out}.}

\item{offset}{Rows to skip before the window. Default 0.}

\item{timeout}{Seconds to allow, or \code{NULL} (the default) to wait: a whole proteome XML takes a
  while.
}

}
\description{
Annotate a stored MetaMorpheus protein-group table with Gene Ontology terms: one row per (group, term) that any member holds, directly or through an ancestor, with no member privileged.

Wraps mzLib's \code{GoGroupAnnotator} over a stored protein-group table
(\code{ProteinGroupFromTsv.ToGoAnnotationGroups}). For each group it returns one row per GO term that
\strong{any} member holds - directly, or by propagation up \code{is_a} and \code{part_of} - and each row names
the members that carry it. Nothing is collapsed: MetaMorpheus picks no leading protein, so the
table is the union, and the views people usually want are filters on its rows.
}
\details{
\strong{Every non-decoy group gets at least one row.} A group with no term gets a single row whose
\code{annotation_status} says why: \code{"no_go_terms"} (its members have none), \code{"no_entry"} (a member is
not in the database - annotate against the database the search used), or \code{"contaminant"}.
Decoy groups get none.

\strong{Pin the ontology.} Terms and their ancestors change between GO releases, so a result means
something only relative to one go.obo. This reads the file you name and never downloads one:
fetch a release on purpose with \code{\link{proteins_update_go}}, keep the file, and record \code{go$sha256}
with your results.
}
\value{
An \code{mzlibr_go_annotations}:

  - \code{annotations}, a data.frame with one row per (group, term) in the returned window, under
    mzLib's own \code{GoAnnotationTsv} column names and order (\code{column_names}). \code{accession_used},
    \code{accession_direct}, \code{accession_inherited}, \code{evidence} and \code{entrapment_members} are list
    columns of character vectors; \code{evidence_by_member} is a list column of named lists, member to
    its own evidence codes. \code{go_id}, \code{go_name}, \code{aspect}, \code{inherited} and \code{propagated} are \code{NA}
    on a term-less row. \code{n_members} and \code{n_with} count proteins (members); \code{n_with} is 0 on a
    term-less row. \code{q_value} is the group's q-value, a fraction (0 to 1), never filtered on.
  - \code{group_count} groups annotated (every non-decoy group, each once); \code{table_row_count} rows in
    the table read, decoys included; \code{decoy_group_count} decoy groups skipped.
  - \code{row_count} rows in the whole table; \code{returned_count} rows in \code{annotations}; \code{offset} rows
    skipped; \code{truncated} is \code{TRUE} when \code{limit} or \code{offset} left rows out.
  - Provenance: \code{groups_file} and \code{groups_file_sha256}; \code{annotation_database} (\code{path},
    \code{file_type}, \code{reader}, \code{protein_count}, \code{sha256} of the decompressed database, \code{caveats});
    \code{go} (\code{source_file_name}, \code{sha256}, \code{release}, \code{term_count}); and \code{header}, mzLib's \code{#!}
    header as a named character vector. \strong{Its counters count groups at q <= 0.01, not rows.}
  - \code{skip_unknown_go_ids}, \code{unresolved_go_ids}, \code{caveats}.
  - \code{written} (\code{path}, \code{row_count}) and \code{categories_written} (\code{path}), or \code{NULL} when not asked.
  - \code{categories}, or \code{NULL} without \code{category_map}: \code{map_name}, \code{map_version},
    \code{source_file_name}, \code{sha256}, \code{anchor_count}, \code{row_count}, and \code{records}, one row per (term,
    category, subcategory). \code{subcategory} is \code{NA} where the term reaches only the category's own
    anchor; a term under no anchor has no row. Join to \code{annotations} on \code{go_id}.

}
\section{The views are filters, not options}{


- \strong{Consensus} - every member carries the term: \code{n_with == n_members}.
- \strong{Direct annotations only}: \code{!propagated}.
- \strong{No borrowing}: \code{!inherited}. An isoform (\code{P04406-2}) or sequence variant (\code{P04406_A20T})
  absent from the database takes its entry's terms and is listed in \code{accession_inherited}; an
  isoform can differ from its entry in cellular component, which is why the row says so.

}
