\section{Caveats}{
\itemize{
\item The table is the UNION over a group's members, never a pick: MetaMorpheus chooses no leading protein. Consensus (n_with == n_members), direct-only (propagated false) and no-borrowing (inherited false) are filters on the rows.
\item Every non-decoy group gets at least one row; a group with no term gets one term-less row whose annotation_status says why. Decoys get none.
\item The header counters count groups at q <= 0.01, not rows; the rows are unfiltered and every group is present.
\item Pin the ontology: terms and ancestors change between releases. This verb reads only an existing go.obo and never downloads one; record go.sha256 with the results.
\item mzlib_release in the header is 'none' and mzlib_version is 1.0.0+<commit>, because the bridge builds mzLib from source at the pinned commit; the commit names the release.
\item An isoform or variant member absent from the database (or present without GO of its own) borrows its entry's terms and is listed in accession_inherited; an isoform can differ from its entry in cellular component, which is why the row says so.
}
}
